37-- The implemented opening uses a 4-move `sheetCamera.ts` shot list, bounded smoothstep, registration hold `t=0.40–1`, `orbitStart .52→.72`, a post-separation `lightSweep`, and HUD chrome only after `.12`. Paper flex is profile-derived (`max 0.003 m`, 4 mm subdivision) and shared across paper/ink/fills/troika text; lite is ×0.45 and proof/reduced is flat. [Task 1]
38-- `drawingCache.ts` hashes position bytes plus layout and `prepareDrawingCache()` fetches `/drawing/jgun-sheet-v1.json.gz` with live-bake fallback. The asset was not generated. `profile.ts`'s offscreen DPR double-application was fixed by using render-target pixels and restoring state with `try/finally`. [Task 1]
39-- `qualityStore.detectWebGL2()` intentionally creates a 300×150 probe canvas and calls `loseContext()`; context-loss instrumentation must exclude disconnected probe canvases. Under `prefers-reduced-motion`, Lenis/ScrollTrigger never mount, so browser harnesses must not require scroll/camera settling. [Task 2]
40:- The 2026-09-26 docs mark the ANSI C/shockwave opening historical; active opening is a 0.80×0.50 m vellum sheet. On a later owner-requested commit, stage JG-035 paths only and include the matching doc updates. [Task 2]
