`CameraRig` writes `probe.cameraSampleTime = runtime.frame.time` and `probe.cameraSampleStamp = state.clock.elapsedTime` on every frame during inspection!
And `InspectionDriver` at `useFrame` priority `-10` in `InspectionScene.tsx`:
```ts
runtime.sample(inspection.time)
integration.sampledTime = runtime.frame.time
integration.sampleStamp = state.clock.elapsedTime
```
When playing, `InspectionDriver` runs at `-10`, sampling `inspection.time` into `runtime.frame.time`, and `integration.sampledTime` gets that value and `sampleStamp` gets `state.clock.elapsedTime`.
Then later in the frame loop (default priority 0), `CameraRig` runs and does:
`probe.cameraSampleTime = runtime.frame.time; probe.cameraSampleStamp = state.clock.elapsedTime`.
So within the same frame (clock.elapsedTime is identical across useFrame callbacks in the same frame!), both `sampledTime` === `cameraSampleTime`, and `sampleStamp` === `cameraSampleStamp`!

