Let's examine how the retry logic at the end and `report.cases` works.
Notice:
"Each run must write a fresh report.json (no appending across runs) with one entry per case."
In the current code:
`runCase` pushes to `report.cases` inside each `caseOrderingReadiness()`, etc.
When `runCase` retries:
`attempt` 1 calls `fn()`, which does `report.cases.push(result)`.
If tainted, `attempt` 2 calls `fn()`, which pushes AGAIN to `report.cases`!
And in `report.gates`, it filters `!c.superseded`, but `report.cases` has multiple items with duplicate names!
And furthermore, if any case fails without a navigation (e.g. timeout or exception), it didn't retry or it stayed in `report.cases`.
Most importantly, `report.json` in the previous run had duplicate cases because:
Each run of `caseCensusLifecycle` pushes `result`, and then returns `[result, ...subResults]`, and pushes them!
Wait! Look at `caseCensusLifecycle`:
```js
