Look at `src/scene/inspection/ringRuntime.ts:202`:
`if (typeof location !== 'undefined' && new URLSearchParams(location.search).has('inspectionProof')) global.__inspectionProof = proof`
And when is `ringRuntime` created?
When the ring inspection is entered and loaded!
And line 190:
`if (typeof window !== 'undefined' && global.__inspectionProof === proof) delete global.__inspectionProof`
When the inspection is unmounted or disposed, `__inspectionProof` is DELETED!
Now look at why `window.__inspectionProof` was undefined in `seek`:
In `seek`:
```js
await page.waitForFunction(() => Boolean(window.__inspectionProof), null, { timeout: 15000 })
await page.evaluate(({ time, entryElapsed }) => window.__inspectionProof.seek(time, entryElapsed), { time, entryElapsed })
```
Wait! What if in between `waitForFunction` and `page.evaluate`, or if `waitForFunction` evaluated `Boolean(window.__inspectionProof)` and returned true, but then in `evaluate` `window.__inspectionProof` was undefined, OR `seek` was called in `ring-rendering` when `window.__inspectionProof` wasn't ready or was destroyed?
